### Is there any post-independence census (such as the 1963 census) that provides a more accurate retroactive estimate of Nigeria's population at the time of independence?
Answer: No, the search result indicates that post-independence censuses—such as the 1962 and 1963 counts—were heavily politicized and manipulated for regional advantage, making them unreliable for accurate retroactive estimates. As the article notes, "there had never been a credible census in Nigeria," and the data has been "weaponized" since independence.

Source URL: https://qz.com/africa/1221472/the-story-of-how-nigerias-census-figures-became-weaponized

